      "description": "Watch Sunderland vs AZ highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 16, 2026. The UEFA Europa League returned to the spotlight on 2026-09-16 as Sunderland and AZ faced off in a highly anticipated group stage matchup. Both sides entered the contest looking to establish dominance in a fixture known for its tactical discipline and physical intensity. A Cautious Opening and Disciplinary Battles The match began with a measured tempo, as both teams displayed a clear respect for one another's tactical setups. However, the physical nature of the contest soon forced the referee into action. Trai Hume of Sunderland received the first yellow card in the 22nd minute, followed closely by teammate Omar Alderete . The tension continued to rise, and AZ were not exempt from the official's notebook, with Ayoub Oufkir cautioned before the break. Despite the frequent whistles, clear-cut chances remained at a premium, leaving the game goalless at the interval after a first half defined more by grit than flair. Le Fee Breaks the Deadlock The second half saw immediate tactical adjustments, with AZ introducing Weslley Pinto for Oufkir . Yet, the momentum shifted decisively in the 65th minute when Pinto was penalized in the area, earning a yellow card and handing the hosts a golden opportunity. Enzo Le Fee stepped up to the spot and calmly dispatched the penalty in the 66th minute to give Sunderland the lead. The goal triggered a flurry of activity on the sidelines. Sunderland opted for a triple change, bringing on Nilson Angulo , Thomas Meunier , and Brian Brobbey to maintain their energy levels. AZ responded by throwing on Calvin Stengs and Jizz Hornkamp in search of an equalizer. Despite the late pressure and a yellow card for Nordi Mukiele , the English side held firm. The final whistle at 90+4 minutes signaled a hard-earned victory for the Black Cats on a night of intense European football."
